{
  "title": "Serum potassium modestly improves frozen cross-cycle HbA1c prediction beyond glucose and red-cell indices",
  "abstract": "In complete-case NHANES adults aged 20\u201379, a frozen 2005\u201306 model adding serum potassium and a potassium\u2013glucose interaction reduced 2007\u201308 HbA1c MEC-weighted MSE from 0.281653 to 0.275962 percentage-points squared (n=4873; gain 0.005691; target-PSU 95% interval 0.002278\u20130.008640, conditional on the source fit). This is small within-program transfer, not incident-diabetes prediction, causal evidence, or independent clinical validation.",
